#! ia 1.0

@law authoring-run-before-claim
  meaning
    says "Declared is not executed, and admission is not truth. Records describe: a contract, law or mandate states what must hold and enforces nothing until an evaluator runs; admission means the records conform, not that they are true. Keep declared, structurally admitted, executed and accepted apart. Never write enforced, verified or passes without the run, and never report a pass for something you did not run in this session; a filtered run that selects nothing can still exit 0, so report it as not found, not pass, and never summarise a failure as a pass with caveats. A rule is enforced only when a contract requirement has success and failure cases whose evaluators run. Ground every claim about an existing thing with path:line, or label it inferred or unknown; read the source, not memory. A case cites a test only after you opened it and confirmed its title; until a test exists the case says unavailable with its gate, which is an honest, complete state. A missing tool means the check is unavailable, never passed."
    answers "What may be claimed about a workspace's records, and what does each claim need behind it?"
  governance
    severity blocking
    requires "Claim enforced, verified or passes only for a run you made in this session and can quote; label every other claim declared, inferred, unknown or unavailable with its gate, and never cite a test you have not opened."
  subject
    subject-word system
    subject-kind definition

@law authoring-stewards-write-their-folders
  meaning
    says "System records are written by each system's steward, inside the folder its stewardship mandate covers, and only with Write or Edit, never with the shell. Nobody else writes a system's records: a lead or an author of workspace instances writes nothing under .ia/src/systems/. IA 3.4.0 renders no steward agents and registers no steward guard (it guards a path only through an authored @hook): the brief's rules, not a hook, keep a steward in its folder, and the absence of a guard is not permission. A write outside a steward's folder is a defect to report; check for it with git log and the diff against the steward's report. Never edit installed package bytes or a cache, never silently reclaim upstream word ownership, and edit hash-pinned files only when you must, with a rehash."
    answers "Who writes a system's records, where, and how is a write outside a steward's folder treated?"
  governance
    severity blocking
    requires "Write a system's records only as its steward, inside the paths its stewardship mandate covers and with file tools; never write under .ia/src/systems/ as anyone but that system's steward, and report any write outside a steward's folder as a defect."
  subject
    subject-word system
    subject-kind definition

@law authoring-no-promotion
  meaning
    says "Don't promote as a side effect, and leave the user's choices to the user. Completing records never changes a component's stage or a seam's stage, closes a gate, changes a decision's status or marks a milestone closed; a proposed or prototype component with real code and tests stays as it is and is reported as a promotion candidate for the human. Product and authority choices are always the user's: frame them with at least two options and what each would change, and never take them; technical ones may be recommended. New systems, stage promotions, gate closures and policy choices go to the user; creating a system needs the user's approval, because in an initialized workspace it is authored by hand. A structural change (a component move, a new system, a minted word) is decided explicitly, recorded where it applies and reported. Never override a user's constraint silently: name the conflict and the reason."
    answers "What may never change as a side effect of completing records, and which choices belong to the user?"
  governance
    severity blocking
    requires "Change no stage, gate, decision status or milestone as a side effect, take no product or authority choice, create no system without the user's approval, and record and report every structural change."
  subject
    subject-word system
    subject-kind definition

@law authoring-probe-never-the-workspace
  meaning
    says "Probe before you write, and never in the real workspace. Admission rules vary by language version: learn them in a scratch copy, never by breaking the real workspace, where it wastes everyone's time and can block other stewards. Never write probe files into the real workspace; probes, captures and surveys run on a temporary copy that is deleted afterwards. Never run the ia on the PATH, which may be an older release, and never npx --no ia, which with no workspace install runs a globally installed CLI; run the CLI the workspace pins, or exactly @inventarch/cli 3.4.0, through the core's ia.mjs or IA_CLI_PATH, and refuse a CLI below 3.x. Do not install, restore, fetch, activate, create organisations or edit access just to answer an authoring question, and never rotate the live capture pair during a read-only survey."
    answers "Where are admission rules learned, and which IA CLI may run?"
  governance
    severity blocking
    requires "Probe, capture and survey only temporary copies of a workspace, never write probe files into it, never run the ia on the PATH or npx --no ia, and never install, restore or capture in a real workspace just to answer a question."
  subject
    subject-word system
    subject-kind definition
